<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuan Shao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 202</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuan Shao was a Chinese warlord of the late Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, from a family of high officials. He led the coalition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dong-zhuo">Dong Zhuo</a> in 190 and became master of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, allying with Wuhuan chiefs such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tadun">Tadun</a>. His defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-guandu">Battle of Guandu</a> in 200 left the north to Cao Cao, and he died in 202.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuan-shao.jpg" alt="Yuan Shao" width="297" height="586" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Plastictv at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yuan_Shao_Portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
